From: mwlaboratories <info@mwlabs.be>
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: scm: leave SDI and the dload cookie alone at probe (sdm845)

On the OnePlus 6 (sdm845), every warm restart from Linux 7.4 ends in
Qualcomm crashdump mode: systemctl reboot, reboot bootloader, with the
reboot mode cold or warm. The PMIC reports a warm reset by PS_HOLD, so
the restart was requested normally and the boot firmware chose dload.
On the same phone, kernel 6.4 restarted fine (journal: next boot 15 s
later).

At probe, v6.4 wrote the download mode cookie only when download mode
was requested, and never disabled SDI. Since v6.11 the probe always
writes "no dump" and, with download mode off, disables SDI
(SDI_CONFIG 1, 0). Restore the v6.4 probe behaviour; the "no dump" write
at shutdown is kept, as v6.4 had it.

Status: hypothesis until tested. The SDI disable is the prime suspect.
---
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c	2026-11-19 18:04:14.583593478 +0100
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c	2026-11-19 18:06:08.044619367 +0100
@@ -2841,12 +2841,20 @@
 	 * will cause the boot stages to enter download mode, unless
 	 * disabled below by a clean shutdown/reboot.
 	 */
-	qcom_scm_set_download_mode(scm, download_mode);
+	/*
+	 * sdm845 (OnePlus 6): at probe, touch the download mode cookie and
+	 * SDI only as v6.4 did (cookie only when download mode is asked for,
+	 * SDI only with qcom,sdi-enabled). On v6.4 warm restarts work; on
+	 * v7.4, with the no-dump write and SDI disable at probe, every warm
+	 * restart (reboot, reboot bootloader) lands in crashdump.
+	 */
+	if (download_mode)
+		qcom_scm_set_download_mode(scm, download_mode);
 
 	/*
 	 * Disable SDI if indicated by DT that it is enabled by default.
 	 */
-	if (of_property_read_bool(pdev->dev.of_node, "qcom,sdi-enabled") || !download_mode)
+	if (of_property_read_bool(pdev->dev.of_node, "qcom,sdi-enabled"))
 		qcom_scm_disable_sdi();
 
 	/*
